.TH HSH 1 "September 2026" "0.1" "Simple Shell Manual"
.SH NAME
hsh \- simple UNIX command line interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a minimal UNIX command language interpreter that reads commands from standard input or from a file and executes them.
.PP
The shell operates in both interactive and non-interactive modes.

.SH INVOCATION
To launch the shell interactively:
.RS
.B $ ./hsh
.br
$
.RE

To run commands non-interactively via pipe:
.RS
.B $ echo "ls -l" | ./hsh
.RE

.SH BUILT-IN COMMANDS
.TP
.B exit [status]
Terminates the shell process. If a numeric status is provided, the shell exits with that integer code; otherwise, it exits with the status of the last executed command.
.TP
.B env
Prints all current environment variables formatted as key=value pairs.

.SH PATH RESOLUTION
If an executable name does not contain a slash (/),
.B hsh
searches through the directories listed in the
.B PATH
environment variable. If the command is not found, an error is printed to stderr and the exit code is set to 127 without calling fork.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on clean exit, 127 when a command is not found, or the exit status of the most recently executed child process.

